            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No, I am afraid not. The goal of \"directory\" category is to provide directory icons based on the directory name, not state. It just so happens that the default one uses \"closed directory\" icon.\r\n\r\nI tried to incorporate \"opened directory\" into 'mini.icons' design, but couldn't find a good way to do it, unfortunately.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">No, I am afraid not. The goal of \"directory\" category is to provide directory icons based on the directory name, not state. It just so happens that the default one uses \"closed directory\" icon.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tried to incorporate \"opened directory\" into 'mini.icons' design, but couldn't find a good way to do it, unfortunately.</p>",
            "bodyText": "No, I am afraid not. The goal of \"directory\" category is to provide directory icons based on the directory name, not state. It just so happens that the default one uses \"closed directory\" icon.\nI tried to incorporate \"opened directory\" into 'mini.icons' design, but couldn't find a good way to do it, unfortunately.",
